# - TK International, official band website, About Us page (opened 2026-10-20): band founded by three friends from Laudat, Dominica; frontline vocalists David "Sonic Tazzy" George, Wayne "Mr Benji N'O" Benjamin and Lennan "Ticky" Matthew; Lennan has the smooth vocals, Benji the raspy chants, Tazzy the high pitched falsettos; Kendel "Killa" Laurent produces all the music, Jeoffrey "JJ Yout" Joseph writes much of the lyrics; album history Big Ting (2000), Fanatik (2003), Sewo, All Out (2006), Pressure (2007), Colours (2008), Allo (2009), Hush Your Mouth (2011), Bubblin (2012); Road March titles with "Please" (2008), "Lock De Gate" (2015), "Roll dat Boom Boom" (2017) and the first ever Peoples Bouyon Road March with "Heat" (2019); "Nous Konnet Vive" official carnival theme 2014; "Still Standing" (2018) after Hurricane Maria; "Toufe" and "Whistle"; WCMF debut 2002, never missed WCMF from 2005; Antilliaanse Feesten 2006 and 2010, Terre de Blues Marie Galante 2012; Commonwealth of Dominica Meritorious Service Award 2022 and Golden Drum Award 2022; community donations.
# - Soca News, "Triple Kay Combo heading to I Love Sewo Jam" (opened 2026-10-20, published 2022-05-16): same frontline trio with Ticky (Lennan Matthew), band from Laudat, nine albums, repertoire spans cadence-lypso, Haitian compas, zouk and bouyon, 2022 singles "Riddim In Your Blood" (Bam Bam) ft Little Boy, "One Call Away" and "One Melody".
# - Mondo Local, WCMF Friday review (search result, 2026-10-20): TK International performing at the World Creole Music Festival on Friday October 24, 2025, with vocalists David "Sonic Tazzy" George, Wayne "Mr. Benji N'O" Benjamin and Lennan "Ticky" Matthew; the band is billed there as "The People's Band".
# Note on the name: after extensive searching (general web, streaming platforms, press), no published source was found that uses the full stage name "Sweet Ticky", and no separate solo discography under that name could be verified. The only "Ticky" documented in bouyon is Lennan "Ticky" Matthew of TK International. This profile therefore covers that documented singer, states the naming gap openly, and invents no solo career. THIN on the solo name, solid on the band record.

